    <h2 id="privacy-collect">Information we collect</h2>
    <p>For paid checkout, we store the selected course, amount, currency, Paystack transaction reference and payment status. Paystack hosts payment authorization; the Academy does not receive or store your mobile money PIN or payment authorization credentials. For trial courses, we store trial start and expiry dates to manage access.</p>
    <p>When you contact us or submit an event registration, webinar registration, career expression of interest, scholarship request, partnership enquiry or accessibility report, we collect the name, email address and details you choose to provide. Career submissions may also include an optional portfolio or professional profile link. We record your consent and the form type so authorised Academy staff can review and respond. If you create a learner account, we collect your name and email address and store a password hash to authenticate your account; we do not store your password in readable form. If you request a course place, we also keep the selected course and the status of your request so Academy staff can review it. For approved courses, we store lesson completion records, quiz scores, assignment submissions and feedback, and course certificates in your learner account to provide learning and show your progress. Public certificate verification pages display the certificate holder’s name, course, issue date and certificate code. If you subscribe to academy updates, we collect your email address and the date you gave consent. Our website host may also process basic technical information, such as your IP address and browser details, in server logs and to limit repeated form submissions.</p>
    <h2 id="privacy-use">How we use it</h2>
    <p>Paystack processes payment authorization and reports transaction results to the Academy so paid course access can be enabled. The transaction reference is retained with your enrollment and payment records for support and reconciliation.</p>
    <p>We use enquiry, application and registration information to respond to you, administer a session or review your expression of interest. We use learner account details, lesson completion records, quiz scores and assignment submissions to provide sign-in, course access, assessment, feedback and progress tracking. We use newsletter addresses to send occasional academy updates; you can ask us to unsubscribe you at any time. We do not sell personal information. Contact submissions, public feature forms, account records, course requests, lesson progress, quiz attempts, assignment work and subscription records are stored in our Firebase Firestore database, accessible to authorised academy staff. When configured, relevant form details are also passed to Resend to deliver an email notification to the Academy.</p>
    <p>Contact forms and newsletter sign-up are separate: asking us a question does not subscribe you to updates. The newsletter form asks for your consent and provides an unsubscribe process.</p>
    <h2 id="privacy-retention">Retention and security</h2>
    <p>We keep enquiries only for as long as needed to handle the request, maintain appropriate business records and meet legal obligations. We keep newsletter details until you unsubscribe or request deletion. We use access controls and reasonable technical safeguards; no internet transmission or storage system can be guaranteed completely secure.</p>
    <h2 id="privacy-choices">Your choices</h2>
    <p>We use essential cookies to keep learner sign-in secure, remember your language selection and save your cookie choice. The session and cookie-choice cookies are protected with HttpOnly and SameSite settings, and use Secure when served over HTTPS. You can accept the cookie notice or cancel to decline optional cookies; essential cookies remain active. We do not currently use advertising or analytics cookies.</p>
    <p>You may ask to access, correct or delete personal information you sent us, or unsubscribe from updates, subject to applicable law. Contact <a href="mailto:hello@techworld.academy">hello@techworld.academy</a> with your request.</p>
    <h2 id="privacy-children">Children and third parties</h2>
    <p>This website is intended for a general audience and is not designed to collect information from children. Our forms send information to Firebase for storage and, when configured, to Resend for contact email delivery. Processing by these providers is subject to their respective terms and privacy commitments.</p>
    <h2 id="privacy-changes">Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy as our services change. The latest version will appear on this page. Questions can be sent to <a href="mailto:hello@techworld.academy">hello@techworld.academy</a>.</p>
